Z||000000||JohnnyK||10-06-2001||06:26 PM||||Is this a common adapter? (Perhaps someone has one here?) I'm going to put a newer GM stereo into an older car (91 van) and the 91 van has a stereo with the Fiero-type connections. So, is it fairly easy to get a adapter that goes from older stereo connection to newer connection?||||reg||1
Z||000001||LarryB||10-06-2001||06:47 PM||||John, I think those adapter kits are available at Walmart.  The new radio has the smaller antenna jack and the van has the older bigger one?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||10-06-2001||07:52 PM||||Not the antenna jack, but the other one(s). On my old ones, I think there was an antanna jack, and then one for power and one for sound. This one is more, smaller jacks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-06-2001||08:02 PM||||The adaptor to put a newer GM/Delco/Delphi radio into an older GM product are available thru the dealers and some aftermarket outlets. The part number from GM is here someplace. use search. It didn't cost a whole lot of $ as I recall. It included everyting you needed electrical I think.<P>The generic adapters of aftermarket radios to go into various cars are available anywhere but the GM-GM set isn't as common.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||10-07-2001||11:27 AM||||Try this one...<BR> <A HREF="http://mnrelectronics.com/par1612to21p.html" TARGET=_blank>http://mnrelectronics.com/par1612to21p.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Orden||10-09-2001||02:16 PM|||| If you can find a Metra dealer in town. You can use 2 adapters. first to adapt to factory plug is part# 7016771 then add to that the new plug for new radio is part#711858. Hope this helps<P>||||reg||3
Z||000006||frontal lobe||10-09-2001||03:59 PM||||I'm with you, JohnnyK.  My cassette doesn't work in the Fiero, and the radio only intermittently.  So I went on e-bay and got a newer gm am/fm cassette for $25 because my speakers aren't great anyway and I'll mostly just use the radio.  So I was hoping to get off cheap, AND THEN THE ADAPTER WAS AS MUCH AS THE STUPID RADIO!<P>So I was hoping to find some best buy or walmart generic one, too, but broke down and got a gm one.||||reg||1
